cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SAFra, please cite it as below."
title: "SAFra: life-cycle carbon calculator for Alcohol-to-Jet SAF from Brazilian ethanol"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-github-user>/safra"
url: "https://<your-github-user>.github.io/safra/"
abstract: >-
  SAFra is a browser-based screening tool that estimates the well-to-wake
  carbon intensity of Alcohol-to-Jet sustainable aviation fuel from Brazilian
  sugarcane and corn ethanol, using state-level agricultural inventories,
  alternative plant configurations, hydrogen supply routes and land-use change
  accounting methods, and benchmarks the results against CORSIA default values,
  US corn pathways and published life cycle assessments.
keywords:
  - sustainable aviation fuel
  - alcohol-to-jet
  - life cycle assessment
  - ethanol
  - Brazil
  - CORSIA
authors:
